# R6-2 (3) (steps/receiver-routes-census-20261010.md, cluster 4): a merge result body field declared without a value --
# `int: w`, `size_t: s`, `char: c` -- is the field's cell holding an unknown value, stored by nothing at construction (the
# author, q56; as the typed operand without a value, RR2d-2), read by the common body construction (K03 RECEIVE-OUTPUT:
# `int: i` is a data declaration).  The program assigns each and reads it back, in a method and at the root.  Exit 7;
# 81..84 name the failing read.
Model:
    size_t: x 1U
end: Model

fn: m () int
    S: merge: Model
        int: w
        char: c
    end: merge
    S\w: 5
    S\c: 'k'
    if: S\w != 5 || S\c != 'k'
        return: 81
    return: 7
end: m

R: merge: Model
    int: w
    size_t: s
end: merge
R\w: 6
R\s: 2U
int: code m()
if: R\w != 6
    code: 82
if: R\s != 2U
    code: 83
if: R\x != 1U
    code: 84
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
